/-!
# Singular point geometry and starred generation in G.2.6

The original marked point is singular, its stabilizer is precisely the
U-image, and the nonorthogonal right conjugate under the original g gives
`I* = (LU)*`. The ordered symmetric comparison carries the actual L-image
to A₃ × A₃ and the actual U-image to a Sylow elementary four-group, including
its two factor intersections. All conclusions use the unchanged source
hypothesis and the original star projection. Model.Maps supplies the existing
residual lift from starred generation to I = LU.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, G.2.6, printed p.336, PDF p.347.
-/
